Package: hsquared
Title: R Interface for Julia-Backed Quantitative-Genetic Models
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Shinichi", "Nakagawa", , "itchyshin@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides the R-facing interface for an open quantitative-genetic
    modelling system backed by the HSquared.jl Julia engine. Experimental
    package: the first CRAN release targets 0.5.0, not 1.0.0. Version 0.1 fits
    the univariate Gaussian animal model (y ~ fixed + animal(1 | id, pedigree =
    ped)) by restricted maximum likelihood and returns heritability, variance
    components, breeding values, and standard extractors. Default fitting
    requires a local Julia and HSquared.jl; use hs_control(engine = "validate")
    to preview the model contract without fitting. What you may report is
    listed on the package article 'Can I fit and report this?', not in
    validation_status(), which is a developer evidence table. Uncertainty
    intervals are experimental and not coverage-calibrated. Genomic,
    single-step, SNP-BLUP,
    repeatability, and two-effect animal models fit through opt-in,
    experimental engine paths; multivariate cbind() animal models route on the
    default call but are likewise experimental and not covered;
    non-Gaussian (poisson/binomial) models fit through an opt-in
    experimental engine path and report no heritability; factor-analytic
    models remain planned.
